1
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:48,000
Right foot.

2
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,000
Xue,

3
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,060
you go on upstairs.

4
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,920
I'm going out to buy a few things.

5
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,590
All right,

6
00:01:59,789 --> 00:02:00,430
I'm off.

7
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:01,070
Okay.

8
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,430
Be careful, okay?

9
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,730
You'd better head back.

10
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:05,590
Want me to walk you up?

11
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,870
No need, go on back.

12
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:07,430
Bye.

13
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,000
I'll be off, too, Uncle Gong.

14
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,980
What's wrong, Uncle Gong?

15
00:02:48,470 --> 00:02:50,000
You two should get married.

16
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:56,520
Get married?

17
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,910
What, you don't want to?

18
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,120
Forget I said anything.

19
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,840
I do! I do!

20
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:02,000
I really do!

21
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:03,470
More than anything!

22
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,240
I just...
don't you think it's a little soon?

23
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,150
She really

24
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,590
likes you,

25
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:13,400
and you

26
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:16,910
clearly care about her, too.

27
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,520
I can see that.

28
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,280
I've been observing you

29
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:25,120
for quite some time now.

30
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,930
You're honest and decent.

31
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,190
A good young man.

32
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,400
My family's

33
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,800
not well-off.

34
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:43,120
I'm just worried that...

35
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:51,960
These days,

36
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:54,370
as long as you're willing to work hard,

37
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:56,970
you'll always find a way
to make a living.

38
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:59,190
As for material things and all that,

39
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,910
I don't need any of it.

40
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,150
No bride price, no engagement gifts,

41
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:05,080
none of that nonsense.

42
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,140
I have just one condition:

43
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,769
you have to treat her well.

44
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,800
You have to treat her

45
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:24,830
even better than I do.

46
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:29,190
Uncle Gong,

47
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:31,570
I promise you this:

48
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:34,390
as long as I, Jia Xin, am breathing,

49
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:35,950
I'll never let Xue suffer

50
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:37,350
a single bit of hardship.

51
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,720
I may not have much right now,

52
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,190
but I'll work hard.

53
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:43,400
Things will only get better from here.

54
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,270
If I ever break this promise,

55
00:04:45,270 --> 00:04:47,400
may I meet the same fate as this bottle!

56
00:04:54,310 --> 00:04:55,830
You two really need

57
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,290
to read fewer martial arts novels.

58
00:05:00,830 --> 00:05:01,600
President,

59
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,310
why'd you bring me here

60
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:04,830
in the middle of the night?

61
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,560
The hospital's been sealed off.

62
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,220
We're trespassing, you know.

63
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
I brought you here

64
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,720
to talk business.

65
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:18,920
You need to be here

66
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:20,480
to really get the feel of it.

67
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:22,120
What do you mean?

68
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:24,090
Is the hospital reopening?

69
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,030
Something like that.

70
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,240
That's wonderful!

71
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,780
I can finally go back to my office.

72
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:34,510
You have no idea

73
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,310
how miserable I've been at home

74
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:37,120
all these days.

75
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,720
Whenever I'm at the hospital,

76
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,390
I...

77
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:40,510
I sleep like a baby

78
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:41,510
as long as I'm at the hospital.

79
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:44,110
I just keep nodding off,
one nap after another.

80
00:05:44,159 --> 00:05:45,390
You can forget

81
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:47,240
about going back to those days.

82
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,240
What?

83
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,830
The hospital's reopening,

84
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:53,510
but

85
00:05:54,070 --> 00:05:55,310
I'm getting fired?

86
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:59,230
What... what do you mean?

87
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,720
I didn't do it on purpose!

88
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,190
I got so excited that I sat down
without even realizing it.

89
00:06:05,190 --> 00:06:05,750
Please,

90
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:06,610
take your seat.

91
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,190
Please, take your seat.

92
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:08,190
I-I'll always follow your lead.

93
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:08,750
Please.

94
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,750
Go ahead and sit down.

95
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:12,480
I-I won't.

96
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,410
I can't sit here.

97
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:14,870
Go ahead and sit down.

98
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:15,830
I can't...

99
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,000
So you do want that seat after all.

100
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,560
No, no, no!

101
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,160
I...

102
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:29,830
Please,

103
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:30,560
take your seat.

104
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,960
I'm not taking that seat.

105
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,830
I r-really didn't

106
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,190
m-mean to earlier.

107
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:37,930
I was just so happy.

108
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,390
Did you really mean

109
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:43,090
what you said earlier?

110
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:44,190
Absolutely.

111
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,000
I meant

112
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,870
every word.

113
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:46,800
J-Just say the word.

114
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,130
What do you need me to do?

115
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,430
I want to put you

116
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:54,630
in the hot seat.

117
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:57,790
Why put me in the hot seat?

118
00:06:58,630 --> 00:06:59,390
Am I supposed to be
Weslie, the Pleasant Goat

119
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:00,720
while you play Wolffy?

120
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:02,070
It's not that bad.

121
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,360
I'll be Weslie, the Pleasant Goat,

122
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,360
and you'll be Slowy, the Mayor Goat.

123
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,160
Wait, what does that
have to do with anything?

124
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,720
You've lost me.

125
00:07:12,190 --> 00:07:13,000
Can you explain

126
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:13,800
what you mean?

127
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,270
Although I've been

128
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:19,510
in talks with the company
taking over Xiaoximen Hospital,

129
00:07:19,510 --> 00:07:20,390
I can't expect

130
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:21,870
everything to go my way.

131
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,720
That's true.

132
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,820
There are bound to be changes,

133
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,120
especially when it comes to personnel.

134
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:31,950
So, what are you saying?
Am I the one

135
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,810
who's going to take the fall here?

136
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,830
Hello,

137
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:40,190
President.

138
00:07:40,950 --> 00:07:41,950
I'm back.

139
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,330
I know my sudden disappearance

140
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,190
caused a lot of trouble and frustration

141
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:48,950
for the hospital

142
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,100
and everyone here.

143
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:51,090
I'm truly sorry.

144
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:54,190
I sincerely apologize to you

145
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,490
and the whole team.

146
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,430
I just wanted to say

147
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:01,870
I'm sorry.

148
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,000
I also brought back

149
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,480
a few local specialties

150
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,540
from the Greater Khingan Mountains.

151
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,800
They're for you and everyone else.

152
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,630
Let me know when you're free,

153
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:20,800
and I'll bring them over.

154
00:08:23,830 --> 00:08:24,630
Thank you.

155
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,170
What are you doing here?

156
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:03,080
Sir,

157
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:05,150
could I borrow your bucket and broom

158
00:10:05,150 --> 00:10:06,360
for a moment?

159
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:54,440
Um,

160
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:56,800
are you Li Zhongling's son?

161
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,870
You know my mom?

162
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,670
I don't know your mom.

163
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,600
I just know she came here twice a year,

164
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:07,320
once in the twelfth lunar month
and once around Qingming.

165
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:09,480
She always stayed here until quite late.

166
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,440
Most people don't spend

167
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:12,960
that long here.

168
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:17,150
I didn't even know her name
until this year,

169
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,030
when they added another name

170
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:20,550
to this gravestone.

171
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:26,030
Sir,

172
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,360
how long have you been working here?

173
00:11:28,870 --> 00:11:31,000
About 15 or 16 years, maybe 17.

174
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:32,960
I've lost count.

175
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,390
Then you've probably known
more dead people

176
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:36,990
than I've known living ones.

177
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,750
Watch your mouth, kid!

178
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,510
I shouldn't have lent you that bucket.

179
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:43,110
And now you're insulting me!

180
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,220
Are there many people like my mom?

181
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:47,770
A few years back,

182
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,910
there was someone who cried
even more than your mom did.

183
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:52,270
Plenty of people have come and gone

184
00:11:52,270 --> 00:11:53,390
over the years,

185
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,550
but not many

186
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:57,960
are like your mom.

187
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:05,320
Then I'll be just like my mom.

188
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,510
I'll come once in the twelfth lunar month

189
00:12:07,510 --> 00:12:09,390
and once around Qingming every year.

190
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:11,120
Why are you telling me all this?

191
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,140
What does it have to do with me?

192
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,960
Sir, I have to go.

193
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,320
I wish you a long and healthy life.

194
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:41,000
And if you ever get sick,

195
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,910
don't forget to come see me.

196
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:43,150
Are you crazy?

197
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,530
Who are you? Why would I come to you?

198
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,360
I'm a doctor

199
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,690
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

200
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,440
My mom is Li Zhongling,

201
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,200
my dad is Liu Chunsheng,

202
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:56,120
and my younger brother is Liu Zhengguang.

203
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:57,970
My name is Liu Zhengliang.

204
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,510
I have a family.

205
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,720
Zhou Zheng has made peace with it,

206
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,630
and so have I.

207
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,750
Some things,

208
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:08,630
no matter how hard you fight them
your whole life,

209
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:09,670
may never go away.

210
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:12,800
Maybe it's better to free yourself

211
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:14,360
and let those things be.

212
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,920
Keep living your life

213
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:17,290
as you always have.

214
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,570
Maybe the snow in my life

215
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,750
will fall forever.

216
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,320
But that doesn't mean
I have to wait for it to stop

217
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,580
before I step outside.

218
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:47,870
You're here?

219
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:50,840
Well,

220
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:53,000
I wanted to show you something.

221
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,000
What is it?

222
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:56,670
Sit down. I'll show you.

223
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:57,360
Here.

224
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:11,080
Come on, take a look.

225
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,630
Did they go on a trip?

226
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,840
Pink took his mom on a trip.

227
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,440
He just sent me these photos.

228
00:14:19,510 --> 00:14:20,570
That's wonderful.

229
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:22,630
He also told me

230
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:24,960
he'd told his mom all about his condition.

231
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,250
Guess what she said?

232
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:28,320
What?

233
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,630
She said she'd known all along.

234
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,750
Look how happy they are.

235
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:42,480
See?

236
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:47,630
You'd never guess
he was feeling unwell, would you?

237
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:48,510
He also told me

238
00:14:48,510 --> 00:14:50,510
he's going to keep smiling like this

239
00:14:50,510 --> 00:14:52,170
until the very end of his life.

240
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:00,920
You're going to make me cry.

241
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:09,150
There's something else.

242
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,840
No need to look for the freezer anymore.

243
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:14,100
We're calling off the exposure therapy.

244
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,080
I've got things to take care of
at the hospital,

245
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,080
so I'll head back.

246
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:31,630
My phone.

247
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,200
Mrs. Mi Si.

248
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,650
What's going on?

249
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,840
What did he do?

250
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,360
Why are you so happy?

251
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:51,870
I just...

252
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,030
I can't even find the words,

253
00:15:54,030 --> 00:15:54,320
Mom.

254
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,920
He said he doesn't
need the treatment anymore.

255
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:58,550
Really?

256
00:16:00,270 --> 00:16:01,720
Does that mean our family's life

257
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:03,510
can finally go back to normal?

258
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:36,480
Last time, they said the place
might shut down.

259
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:37,550
This time, who knows?
They might just

260
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:39,750
lay everyone off, pay out the severance,

261
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:40,750
and call it quits.

262
00:16:41,630 --> 00:16:43,440
How much longer do we have?

263
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:53,910
Is Chen Junnan back?

264
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:57,410
He's been back for days.

265
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,140
Didn't he tell you?

266
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:00,870
No.

267
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,670
I only found out

268
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:03,930
because my dad told me.

269
00:17:04,349 --> 00:17:05,550
How did your dad know?

270
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:07,440
I have no idea

271
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:09,240
when those two got back in touch.

272
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:12,880
Uncle Che really is something else.

273
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:14,589
Huang,

274
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,240
didn't you let Chen Junnan know?

275
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,770
How come he hasn't shown up?

276
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,240
Huang,

277
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:24,410
what are you doing?

278
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,980
What, are you cold?

279
00:17:27,109 --> 00:17:28,270
No, not cold.

280
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:29,750
Then why are you shivering?

281
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:30,440
I'm not.

282
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:32,610
Huang, where's your padded vest?

283
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,370
I'm actually feeling a little hot.

284
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,680
Quite a fire you've got going there.

285
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:37,610
It's not too bad.

286
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:51,240
A month ago,

287
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,880
it was announced that Xiaoximen Hospital

288
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,240
would be shut down.

289
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,440
Today,

290
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,680
I have some latest news

291
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,750
to share with you.

292
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:05,090
Xiaoximen Hospital

293
00:18:06,030 --> 00:18:07,680
has been taken over by Xikang Group,

294
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,790
one of the leading

295
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:12,480
private healthcare providers

296
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,310
in our province.

297
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,640
It will be renamed

298
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:17,590
Xiaoximen Hospital,

299
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:19,510
affiliated with Xikang Medical.

300
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,830
With improvements
in both facilities and services,

301
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:25,070
patients will receive

302
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:26,730
even better care than before.

303
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,930
But before Xiaoximen Hospital

304
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,750
can rise from the ashes,

305
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:41,350
there's one more challenge

306
00:18:41,350 --> 00:18:43,110
we need to address.

307
00:18:43,590 --> 00:18:44,550
Xikang Group

308
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,790
has selected

309
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,790
100 outstanding employees

310
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,590
from its other hospitals

311
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,310
to join Xiaoximen Hospital.

312
00:18:52,310 --> 00:18:53,550
As a result,

313
00:18:57,110 --> 00:18:58,830
there will be

314
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,640
fewer positions available

315
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:04,070
for the existing Xiaoximen staff.

316
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:16,830
I know

317
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:19,960
some of you

318
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,160
have already

319
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,020
found new jobs,

320
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,680
while others

321
00:19:24,110 --> 00:19:26,240
have negotiated severance packages.

322
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,030
The reopening of Xiaoximen Hospital

323
00:19:30,030 --> 00:19:33,680
won't affect those plans.

324
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,030
Over the next day or two,

325
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,290
the hospital president

326
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:41,240
will begin holding
one-on-one meetings with you.

327
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,270
Anyone who wants to stay

328
00:19:43,830 --> 00:19:45,640
can fill out an application form.

329
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,480
The new management team

330
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,720
will then select from among those
who wish to stay.

331
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:50,880
But the reality is,

332
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,720
many of you

333
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:55,160
may not make the cut.

334
00:19:55,550 --> 00:19:56,350
S-Sorry to interrupt,

335
00:19:56,350 --> 00:19:57,350
President,

336
00:19:57,350 --> 00:19:58,880
but may I say something?

337
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Based on what you've just said,

338
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,310
how many positions will be available?

339
00:20:03,310 --> 00:20:05,000
President Long, now
that we're becoming a private hospital,

340
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
will there be any changes to our salaries?

341
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,930
We don't want to end up
doing more work for less money.

342
00:20:10,070 --> 00:20:10,440
President,

343
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,720
what criteria will be used

344
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,720
to select the people who get to stay?

345
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:15,640
One more thing.

346
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:16,640
This really

347
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:17,640
is the last thing.

348
00:20:18,510 --> 00:20:20,480
For various reasons,

349
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:22,880
I'll be serving

350
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,270
as a management consultant

351
00:20:24,270 --> 00:20:25,590
at Xiaoximen Hospital,

352
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:27,450
affiliated with Xikang Medical.

353
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,070
And when I said

354
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:32,790
there would be one-on-one meetings
with the hospital president,

355
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:34,790
I meant the new hospital president.

356
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,020
The new president?

357
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:37,470
Who is the new president?

358
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,740
The new president showed up pretty fast.

359
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:41,110
Now,

360
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,120
Now, let's give a warm round of applause

361
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:47,110
to Comrade Huang Dongsheng,

362
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,070
our acting president

363
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:50,400
for the preparatory period.

364
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,070
Let's hear a few words from him.

365
00:20:52,070 --> 00:20:52,880
Who?

366
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,440
Huang?

367
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:04,100
As long as I get paid, I'm good.

368
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,550
Distinguished

369
00:21:22,270 --> 00:21:23,670
President Long Dongdong

370
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:27,440
and esteemed colleagues.

371
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:33,590
I've been entrusted
with this role at a critical time,

372
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:35,270
and I must say, um,

373
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:37,790
it's a

374
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:42,570
heavy burden to bear. A very heavy burden.

375
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:47,790
But one thing

376
00:21:47,790 --> 00:21:50,200
I can promise is

377
00:21:50,790 --> 00:21:53,270
that I won't

378
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:55,400
let President Long down.

379
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,660
I won't betray the trust
he's placed in me

380
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:58,930
or the... the...

381
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:01,000
his heartfelt repentance.

382
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,440
I mean,

383
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,110
his guidance.

384
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:05,960
Yes, his guidance.

385
00:22:07,350 --> 00:22:09,880
I will live up to his expectations

386
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:15,380
and forge ahead,
no matter how heavy the burden.

387
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:17,160
Reform

388
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,440
is inevitable.

389
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:19,920
It has to happen.

390
00:22:20,070 --> 00:22:21,160
And I believe that,

391
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,350
with all of us

392
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:23,640
working together,

393
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:26,720
we can

394
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,310
breathe new life into Xiaoximen Hospital

395
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:33,680
and help it flourish once again.

396
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:54,880
Do you know what's going on?

397
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,240
Why do they insist
on having one-on-one meetings?

398
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,200
No idea.

399
00:22:57,240 --> 00:22:58,770
They called me, so here I am.

400
00:22:59,270 --> 00:23:01,550
How long has the person before us
been in there?

401
00:23:01,550 --> 00:23:02,790
Quite a while now.

402
00:23:03,350 --> 00:23:04,610
Still hasn't come out?

403
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:06,830
Nope. The door's still closed.

404
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:08,720
Stop scrolling on your phone.

405
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,440
You might not hear them
call your name later.

406
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:12,370
I'm just having a look, that's all.

407
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,420
Hold on, Huang Dongsheng,

408
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,830
what the hell are you talking about?

409
00:23:18,830 --> 00:23:20,290
Do you even hear yourself?

410
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,920
Is that any way to talk?

411
00:23:22,790 --> 00:23:24,120
Who do you think you are?

412
00:23:24,310 --> 00:23:25,640
How am I even

413
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:26,960
supposed to describe someone like you?

414
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:28,070
This job's not easy, is it?

415
00:23:28,070 --> 00:23:28,400
You can say that again.

416
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,590
You're just a nobody

417
00:23:29,590 --> 00:23:30,640
pretending to be

418
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:32,590
some big shot!

419
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:33,960
Wait,

420
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:36,360
when did you even join Xiaoximen Hospital?

421
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:37,920
And when did I join?

422
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:39,110
You think you can compare yourself to me?

423
00:23:39,110 --> 00:23:40,160
Stop acting like some big shot!

424
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:41,360
Quit putting on airs!

425
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:44,400
Let's talk this out calmly.

426
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:45,790
I'm the hospital president.

427
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:46,440
What?

428
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:47,960
What did you say?
I didn't quite catch that.

429
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,030
Say it again.

430
00:23:49,350 --> 00:23:50,790
You're the President?

431
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,270
Just look at the nonsense

432
00:23:52,270 --> 00:23:53,550
you spouted onstage!

433
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:55,350
"Th-th-th...

434
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:56,590
Esteemed...

435
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:59,090
esteemed colleagues at the hospital,

436
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,070
under

437
00:24:00,070 --> 00:24:01,920
President Long's leadership
and... repentance..."

438
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,240
You even said "repentance"!

439
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:04,640
Do you even know what that word means?

440
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:05,970
Have you ever repented?

441
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:07,550
Look,

442
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:09,160
the President is right here,

443
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:10,290
sitting right here!

444
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:12,810
President Long,

445
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,440
you have to stand up for justice!

446
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:15,640
You can't let this man

447
00:24:15,750 --> 00:24:16,960
run wild!

448
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:20,750
If he's forcing you to do this,

449
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:22,350
just blink twice!

450
00:24:23,070 --> 00:24:24,790
I'm no longer the President.

451
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:26,920
Huang is in charge now.

452
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:28,450
I'm just here to assist him.

453
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:29,590
A-Assist him?

454
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:32,410
President Long?

455
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:41,380
How many complaints
have you gotten this month?

456
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,270
Two.

457
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:44,830
That's a lot better than last month.

458
00:24:45,550 --> 00:24:46,950
And you're proud of that?

459
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:48,790
Have you no shame?

460
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:50,400
Boss,

461
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,270
if you have something to say,
just say it.

462
00:24:51,270 --> 00:24:52,640
There's no need to insult me.

463
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,350
Besides, this wasn't

464
00:24:53,350 --> 00:24:54,750
even my fault.

465
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,000
He put down the wrong address,

466
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,480
so I had to deliver the package again.

467
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:59,030
I won't even complain
about the extra trip.

468
00:24:59,030 --> 00:25:00,160
I was just a little late,

469
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:00,920
and he started cursing me out.

470
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,680
So just because he cursed at you,

471
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,200
that gives you the right
to curse him back?

472
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:04,920
Why shouldn't I?

473
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:07,830
Because you're the one
providing the service,

474
00:25:07,830 --> 00:25:09,160
and he's the customer!

475
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,960
So what if he cursed at you?

476
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:12,360
What makes you so special

477
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,960
that you can't even take a little abuse?

478
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:14,750
I'm just doing a service job,

479
00:25:14,750 --> 00:25:16,350
but I still earn my living

480
00:25:16,350 --> 00:25:17,750
through hard work.

481
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,070
Why should I put up
with being mistreated?

482
00:25:19,070 --> 00:25:20,400
I'm no less than him.

483
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,680
He has no right to insult me,

484
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:23,740
and neither do you.

485
00:25:24,750 --> 00:25:26,550
You think I enjoy chewing you out?

486
00:25:26,550 --> 00:25:27,240
If I hadn't

487
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,310
brought a troublemaker

488
00:25:28,310 --> 00:25:29,160
like you on board,

489
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:29,640
would I be dealing

490
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:31,440
with all these problems?

491
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:33,030
If you don't want to work, then get lost!

492
00:25:33,030 --> 00:25:34,640
Go home and live like a king!

493
00:25:35,830 --> 00:25:36,830
Fine, I'm done!

494
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:37,880
What are you gonna do about it?

495
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:38,960
Hit me?

496
00:25:39,310 --> 00:25:40,440
You're practically halfway

497
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,070
to the grave at your age.

498
00:25:41,070 --> 00:25:42,930
You think you can still take me on?

499
00:25:43,110 --> 00:25:43,840
Medicine...

500
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:46,590
medicine.

501
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:48,000
W-What did you say?

502
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:49,720
In the drawer.

503
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:51,400
Quick-acting...

504
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:52,130
Medicine...

505
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:53,770
Q-Q-Quick-acting...

506
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:57,960
Boss!

507
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,400
Boss! Are you okay? Boss!

508
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,070
Boss!

509
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:00,960
Boss!

510
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,550
Boss! Boss!

511
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,480
I... Oh, right. Right.

512
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:07,720
I'm telling you,

513
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:09,070
you've got it all backwards!

514
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:09,510
Hello?

515
00:26:09,510 --> 00:26:10,880
You're abusing your power

516
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,810
and mistreating your colleagues!

517
00:26:13,310 --> 00:26:14,030
Let me find somewhere quiet

518
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:15,000
to talk to you.

519
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:16,090
I'm telling you.

520
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:18,200
Huang Dongsheng?

521
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:19,770
More like Huang the Weasel!

522
00:26:20,310 --> 00:26:21,310
When you call his name,

523
00:26:21,310 --> 00:26:22,350
does he respond?

524
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:23,400
No.

525
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,440
What about the ambulance?
Have you called one?

526
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:27,110
Yes,

527
00:26:27,110 --> 00:26:29,370
b-but it'll be another ten minutes or so.

528
00:26:29,440 --> 00:26:30,110
I-I think I made him so angry

529
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:31,200
that he passed out.

530
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,200
H-He can't

531
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:33,070
be dead, can he?

532
00:26:33,070 --> 00:26:34,350
All right, Liu Zhengguang,

533
00:26:34,350 --> 00:26:35,000
calm down.

534
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,200
He's going to be fine.

535
00:26:36,310 --> 00:26:37,240
Listen to me.

536
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,640
I need you to check his carotid pulse

537
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:40,000
with your fingers,

538
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:42,070
about a centimeter
beside his Adam's apple.

539
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:43,200
Can you feel a pulse?

540
00:26:44,350 --> 00:26:44,960
No.

541
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,270
I... I can't feel anything.

542
00:26:46,270 --> 00:26:47,160
T-There's no pulse.

543
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:48,240
Why don't we just leave him alone

544
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,400
and wait

545
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,460
for the ambulance?

546
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:52,960
W-What do I do?

547
00:26:55,310 --> 00:26:56,590
He needs CPR.

548
00:26:58,070 --> 00:26:59,130
Do exactly as I say.

549
00:26:59,270 --> 00:27:00,880
Lay him flat on the ground,

550
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:02,200
then kneel beside him.

551
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:05,080
I'm kneeling. I'm kneeling.

552
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:06,000
What now?

553
00:27:06,510 --> 00:27:07,920
Place the heel of one hand

554
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:10,000
in the center of his chest,

555
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:11,720
clasp your other hand over it,

556
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,750
and keep your arms straight.

557
00:27:12,750 --> 00:27:14,550
Use your upper body weight to push down.

558
00:27:14,550 --> 00:27:16,160
Compress his chest to a depth
of five to six centimeters,

559
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:17,070
at a rate of 100

560
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:18,030
to 120 compressions per minute.

561
00:27:18,030 --> 00:27:19,000
Got that?

562
00:27:19,070 --> 00:27:19,920
Are you sure

563
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:20,750
this will work?

564
00:27:20,750 --> 00:27:22,400
I'm sure. Trust me.

565
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:23,590
Follow my rhythm.

566
00:27:24,030 --> 00:27:25,160
When I say "down,"

567
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:26,030
you push.

568
00:27:26,590 --> 00:27:27,400
Start now.

569
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:33,270
Down, down, down.

570
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:39,480
Down, down, down.

571
00:27:39,590 --> 00:27:40,720
Keep that rhythm.

572
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:42,000
And remember,

573
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:44,440
keep your arms straight. Don't bend them.

574
00:27:52,590 --> 00:27:53,400
How is he?

575
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:54,590
Any change?

576
00:27:55,310 --> 00:27:56,110
No,

577
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,440
he's still not breathing.

578
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:58,000
He is...

579
00:27:58,070 --> 00:27:59,550
he is turning purple.

580
00:28:01,160 --> 00:28:02,680
After every 30 compressions,

581
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:03,960
give him two rescue breaths.

582
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:05,750
Tilt his head back, lift his chin,

583
00:28:05,750 --> 00:28:06,590
pinch his nose shut,

584
00:28:06,590 --> 00:28:08,550
and breathe into his mouth. Hurry!

585
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,400
I... I did it.

586
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:11,400
Keep going.

587
00:28:11,510 --> 00:28:12,840
Count 30 compressions.

588
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,550
28, 29,

589
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:18,720
30. Stop.

590
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:20,340
Give him two more breaths.

591
00:28:21,830 --> 00:28:22,640
I did it.

592
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:27,960
H-He's breathing!

593
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:28,890
He's breathing!

594
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:30,880
He couldn't catch his breath just now.

595
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:31,480
It was terrifying to watch.

596
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,200
Oh my God!

597
00:28:35,270 --> 00:28:35,880
All right,

598
00:28:36,550 --> 00:28:38,110
turn his head to the side

599
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:39,960
and just wait for the ambulance.

600
00:28:45,790 --> 00:28:47,790
My heart was in my throat.

601
00:28:47,920 --> 00:28:50,510
I really thought something terrible
was going to happen.

602
00:28:50,510 --> 00:28:51,830
I can't believe someone could actually

603
00:28:51,830 --> 00:28:53,000
talk a person through CPR over the phone.

604
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:53,930
That's amazing!

605
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:56,440
Zhengguang,

606
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:58,480
well done!

607
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,900
That's my little brother!

608
00:29:03,310 --> 00:29:05,240
You did a great job guiding me, too.

609
00:29:07,510 --> 00:29:08,770
That's my big brother!

610
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:21,680
Huang,

611
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:24,300
what's that expression on your face?

612
00:29:26,550 --> 00:29:27,110
Well, um...

613
00:29:27,110 --> 00:29:28,550
weren't you planning

614
00:29:28,550 --> 00:29:29,550
to go for your PhD?

615
00:29:30,350 --> 00:29:31,160
I, um,

616
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:32,030
I only submitted my application

617
00:29:32,030 --> 00:29:33,240
in November.

618
00:29:33,790 --> 00:29:34,510
Besides,

619
00:29:34,510 --> 00:29:35,920
what if I don't get in?

620
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,320
I'd still have to keep working,
wouldn't I?

621
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:40,030
Right,

622
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:41,550
but...

623
00:29:41,550 --> 00:29:42,830
here's the thing...

624
00:29:42,830 --> 00:29:43,750
h-here's the thing...

625
00:29:43,750 --> 00:29:46,480
There are more people
than positions available.

626
00:29:47,350 --> 00:29:47,830
If I

627
00:29:47,830 --> 00:29:49,590
offer you the position

628
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:51,400
and you get into the PhD program

629
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,160
and don't come back afterward,

630
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:53,030
then I'll...

631
00:29:53,510 --> 00:29:54,240
I...

632
00:29:54,510 --> 00:29:55,310
No,

633
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:57,680
I'll come back after I finish my PhD.

634
00:29:57,680 --> 00:29:58,790
No, no, no.

635
00:29:58,790 --> 00:29:59,510
I mean,

636
00:29:59,510 --> 00:30:00,000
um,

637
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,000
once you get into the PhD program,
your position will be vacant,

638
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:02,680
and then

639
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:04,680
people will come after me, you know?

640
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:06,180
What are you trying to say?

641
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,160
I... I just mean

642
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:09,480
that if the position becomes vacant,

643
00:30:09,480 --> 00:30:10,920
it'll put me in a really difficult spot.

644
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:11,400
What are you trying to say, then?

645
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:11,920
It's really putting me
in a difficult spot.

646
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:13,240
It's hard, you know?

647
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,070
Very hard.

648
00:30:15,270 --> 00:30:16,480
Are you letting your position
dictate how you think,

649
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:17,240
Huang?

650
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:17,830
Seriously,

651
00:30:17,830 --> 00:30:18,590
why have you changed so much

652
00:30:18,590 --> 00:30:19,440
the moment you became a leader?

653
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:20,720
What kind of leader am I?

654
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:22,520
Tell me, what kind of leader am I?

655
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:23,750
I'm just taking the fall

656
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:24,880
for President Long!

657
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:26,270
Once I've cleaned up

658
00:30:26,270 --> 00:30:27,480
this whole mess,

659
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:28,880
X-Xikang Medical

660
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:29,880
will send over

661
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:31,400
a new president.

662
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:32,830
What do you think

663
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:34,630
I'll get out of being President?

664
00:30:36,830 --> 00:30:39,030
T-Then why did you agree to take the job?

665
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,480
I just wanted to see

666
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:42,400
what it felt like to be a president.

667
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,160
I'd never been one before.

668
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:44,490
And how does it feel now?

669
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:46,830
It's intense.

670
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:55,070
T-This is no job for a human being.

671
00:30:55,480 --> 00:30:56,270
Huang,

672
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:57,790
this was your decision.

673
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:59,990
You have to take responsibility for it.

674
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:01,160
Anyway,

675
00:31:02,070 --> 00:31:04,330
we've been colleagues for so many years.

676
00:31:04,510 --> 00:31:06,070
You know me better than anyone, don't you?

677
00:31:06,070 --> 00:31:06,720
I

678
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:08,030
have never

679
00:31:08,030 --> 00:31:09,690
let Xiaoximen Hospital down.

680
00:31:10,350 --> 00:31:10,880
Then Xiaoximen Hospital

681
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:12,610
shouldn't let me down, either.

682
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:15,480
And neither should you.

683
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,310
Look,

684
00:31:23,310 --> 00:31:24,720
um,

685
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:25,880
just let me...

686
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:27,070
let me think it over.

687
00:31:27,070 --> 00:31:27,830
T-There are

688
00:31:28,070 --> 00:31:29,110
so many people watching.

689
00:31:29,110 --> 00:31:29,910
Can you please

690
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:32,110
show a little support?

691
00:31:36,590 --> 00:31:37,400
Please?

692
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:48,000
Just...

693
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:51,340
just give me a chance to...

694
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:54,270
Mingming.

695
00:31:54,510 --> 00:31:55,070
Hey, don't, don't.

696
00:31:55,070 --> 00:31:56,400
Don't cry. Don't cry...

697
00:32:03,590 --> 00:32:04,640
Don't cry...

698
00:32:17,830 --> 00:32:18,440
This...

699
00:32:18,590 --> 00:32:20,880
This is just downright heartless.

700
00:32:23,350 --> 00:32:23,790
Mom, Dad,

701
00:32:23,790 --> 00:32:26,200
there's something
I want to talk over with you.

702
00:32:26,200 --> 00:32:27,030
Go ahead.

703
00:32:27,790 --> 00:32:30,160
Whatever it is, your dad and I
will support you.

704
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:32,090
I don't want to be a doctor anymore.

705
00:32:36,310 --> 00:32:37,910
You don't want to be a doctor?

706
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,510
You can't just quit being a doctor

707
00:32:39,510 --> 00:32:41,030
after all these years.

708
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:42,880
I think

709
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:44,830
going into medicine was a mistake.

710
00:32:46,070 --> 00:32:47,000
I

711
00:32:47,790 --> 00:32:49,830
need to correct that mistake.

712
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,160
W-Wait,

713
00:32:52,160 --> 00:32:52,830
Chen.

714
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:54,640
Don't get worked up.

715
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,880
You need to give him some time

716
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,410
to process this, don't you?

717
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,200
Look how upset you've made your dad.

718
00:32:59,200 --> 00:32:59,960
Why do you

719
00:33:00,030 --> 00:33:01,890
keep changing your mind on a whim?

720
00:33:03,030 --> 00:33:03,830
Chen Junnan,

721
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:06,920
I support you.

722
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:08,270
What?

723
00:33:09,310 --> 00:33:10,110
Chen,

724
00:33:10,720 --> 00:33:12,050
have you lost your mind?

725
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:13,070
You know, we used to think

726
00:33:13,070 --> 00:33:15,310
being a doctor was a secure,
lifelong career.

727
00:33:15,310 --> 00:33:16,510
The older you got,
the more valuable you became.

728
00:33:16,510 --> 00:33:17,570
What a load of crap.

729
00:33:18,350 --> 00:33:19,960
After doing this for so many years,
I finally realized

730
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:23,550
that you're carrying the weight
of other people's lives in your hands.

731
00:33:23,550 --> 00:33:24,480
You never wanted

732
00:33:25,030 --> 00:33:27,090
to study medicine in the first place.

733
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:29,680
Making you do it was a mistake.

734
00:33:30,590 --> 00:33:32,590
It wasn't your mistake. It was mine.

735
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,830
Back then,

736
00:33:36,110 --> 00:33:37,720
I thought if you became a doctor,

737
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:38,720
I could pull some strings

738
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:40,720
and get you a job when you graduated.

739
00:33:42,030 --> 00:33:43,480
I never stopped to think about you—

740
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,550
whether you liked it

741
00:33:44,550 --> 00:33:46,280
or whether it was right for you.

742
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:50,720
Junnan,

743
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:54,980
while you were away in the mountains,

744
00:33:56,350 --> 00:33:57,950
I had a lot of time to reflect.

745
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,680
And I realized...

746
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:08,280
I realized I'd held you back.

747
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:11,219
More than ten years
of your life are gone.

748
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:12,230
The...

749
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:13,510
The most

750
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:14,670
precious years of your life...

751
00:34:14,670 --> 00:34:16,150
I wasted them.

752
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:18,070
Dad, no... You didn't waste them.

753
00:34:18,070 --> 00:34:18,550
You didn't.

754
00:34:18,550 --> 00:34:20,510
Let me apologize to you again, okay?

755
00:34:20,510 --> 00:34:21,670
No, Dad.

756
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:26,150
I just want to make a fresh start.

757
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:26,920
All right.

758
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:28,710
Junnan,

759
00:34:30,230 --> 00:34:32,360
let's toast with milk instead of wine.

760
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:34,480
Here's a toast to your new journey!

761
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:35,550
Wait, wait, wait!

762
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,000
What is going on here?

763
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:38,070
You two just went back and forth

764
00:34:38,070 --> 00:34:39,730
and made the decision for him?

765
00:34:40,070 --> 00:34:41,670
He studied medicine for all those years,

766
00:34:41,670 --> 00:34:42,960
and now he's just going to quit?

767
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,630
If you're not going to be a doctor,

768
00:34:44,630 --> 00:34:45,960
what are you going to do?

769
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:48,550
Anything.

770
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:50,020
Exactly. Tell her!

771
00:34:50,670 --> 00:34:51,480
I could...

772
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:55,190
I could raise cattle.

773
00:34:55,710 --> 00:34:56,590
Oh, get out of here!

774
00:34:56,590 --> 00:34:58,000
Raise cattle? You?

775
00:34:58,630 --> 00:34:59,480
You can't just go

776
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,000
f-from one extreme to the other!

777
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:01,800
Raise cattle?

778
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:03,070
And cattle...

779
00:35:03,150 --> 00:35:06,680
do you even know how to raise them?
Starting with calves and all?

780
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:18,150
Someone from
the Marine Research Institute called.

781
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:20,150
They said Yaya has fully recovered.

782
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:22,520
You can finally stop worrying now, right?

783
00:35:22,710 --> 00:35:23,550
Who's Yaya?

784
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:26,400
Didn't you name

785
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:27,800
that seal Yaya?

786
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,560
Don't be ridiculous.

787
00:35:30,590 --> 00:35:32,450
Yaya is your childhood nickname.

788
00:35:32,630 --> 00:35:33,710
How could I give a seal

789
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:35,170
your childhood nickname?

790
00:35:37,670 --> 00:35:39,600
I must've remembered wrong, then.

791
00:35:42,280 --> 00:35:43,070
Coming.

792
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,150
Coming.

793
00:35:56,230 --> 00:35:57,320
I'm heading

794
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:59,360
to Beijing in a few days
to discuss a business deal.

795
00:35:59,360 --> 00:36:01,760
I'm planning to leave
in the next day or two.

796
00:36:04,070 --> 00:36:05,190
So, you're giving up being a doctor

797
00:36:05,190 --> 00:36:06,720
to become a business owner?

798
00:36:08,510 --> 00:36:09,320
No,

799
00:36:09,480 --> 00:36:10,150
I just...

800
00:36:11,190 --> 00:36:13,450
I need to figure out something else to do.

801
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,150
Is that why you came here?

802
00:36:23,150 --> 00:36:25,350
Just to tell me you're going to Beijing?

803
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,150
You didn't have to.

804
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,630
You went all the way
to the Greater Khingan Mountains

805
00:36:29,630 --> 00:36:32,160
to see my ex-husband
without even telling me.

806
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:36,800
I'm sorry.

807
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:38,960
I shouldn't have kept it from you.

808
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,490
You don't owe me an apology.

809
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:42,920
You're free to go wherever you want.

810
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:45,150
We're just colleagues.

811
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:47,360
It's not like we're that close.

812
00:36:59,190 --> 00:37:00,850
Has Uncle Che been to Beijing?

813
00:37:02,150 --> 00:37:03,800
No. Why?

814
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:05,490
I'd like to take him with me.

815
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:08,280
Why?

816
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:09,760
Didn't he used to say

817
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:11,190
he had a job in Beijing?

818
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:12,840
Maybe taking him there

819
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:13,960
would help

820
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:16,450
with his condition.

821
00:37:18,510 --> 00:37:19,320
It won't work.

822
00:37:19,670 --> 00:37:21,470
I've suggested it to him before,

823
00:37:21,630 --> 00:37:23,030
but he flat-out refused.

824
00:37:23,510 --> 00:37:24,320
He...

825
00:37:24,670 --> 00:37:27,320
He said he'd been sent here
by the organization on a mission,

826
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:29,360
and that he couldn't return to Beijing
until the time was right.

827
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:31,560
We can't exactly force him to go, can we?

828
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:36,500
I didn't know the whole story.
Never mind, then.

829
00:37:37,190 --> 00:37:40,250
The tale of the golden millet dream
on the road to Handan

830
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:43,960
reminds us not to envy Lu Sheng's
fleeting dream of glory.

831
00:37:49,590 --> 00:37:50,720
Commissioner Chen.

832
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:53,140
Commissioner Chen, you're here!

833
00:37:54,550 --> 00:37:55,360
Does this mean

834
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:56,960
the time has finally come

835
00:37:56,960 --> 00:37:58,440
for me to return to Beijing
and give my report?

836
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:00,440
Comrade Xiaobo told you, didn't he?

837
00:38:03,320 --> 00:38:05,920
The day I've been waiting for
has finally come!

838
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:23,230
What's going on?

839
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:25,400
Why'd you call me out here
in such a hurry?

840
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:25,840
I have to get back to the hospital

841
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:27,300
for some overtime in a bit.

842
00:38:29,920 --> 00:38:31,450
Do you remember this place?

843
00:38:33,550 --> 00:38:34,670
Of course I do.

844
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,110
Didn't we used to come here

845
00:38:36,110 --> 00:38:38,240
and play all the time when we were kids?

846
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:42,590
The last time we came here

847
00:38:43,590 --> 00:38:45,520
was before you left for Guangzhou.

848
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:50,400
I wonder if that little shop over there

849
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:51,360
is still open.

850
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:54,230
It's gone.

851
00:39:03,920 --> 00:39:05,720
I'm planning to move to Beijing.

852
00:39:07,070 --> 00:39:08,000
What do you mean?

853
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:10,600
You're not going to be a doctor anymore?

854
00:39:11,590 --> 00:39:12,550
Ever since I

855
00:39:12,550 --> 00:39:14,150
failed to save that patient,

856
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:15,630
I've been terrified every time

857
00:39:15,630 --> 00:39:17,490
I have to attempt resuscitation.

858
00:39:18,150 --> 00:39:20,110
Even when I went
to the Greater Khingan Mountains

859
00:39:20,110 --> 00:39:22,710
and saw those animals
barely clinging to life,

860
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,630
I was so scared

861
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:26,360
I was shaking.

862
00:39:28,590 --> 00:39:30,360
But that's when I realized

863
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:33,880
what scares me most

864
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:35,940
is having someone else's life

865
00:39:36,110 --> 00:39:37,360
in my hands.

866
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:40,220
You're different from me.

867
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:41,440
You're always the first

868
00:39:41,440 --> 00:39:43,440
to rush in when a patient needs help,

869
00:39:44,070 --> 00:39:45,730
no matter how things turn out.

870
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,840
Can you stop making me
sound like some kind of hero?

871
00:39:47,840 --> 00:39:48,550
I'm not.

872
00:39:48,550 --> 00:39:50,280
I'm not as amazing as you think.

873
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,710
I just can't face the moment

874
00:39:56,590 --> 00:39:57,760
when someone dies.

875
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:03,940
We're the same in that way.

876
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:07,880
I just chose to run away.

877
00:40:10,070 --> 00:40:12,070
If I run away, I don't have to face it.

878
00:40:12,550 --> 00:40:14,150
And if I don't have to face it,

879
00:40:15,550 --> 00:40:17,230
I don't have to feel

880
00:40:18,190 --> 00:40:19,650
that helplessness again.

881
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:23,760
I understand.

882
00:40:25,480 --> 00:40:26,280
I really do.

883
00:40:33,510 --> 00:40:35,640
Have you really thought this through?

884
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:38,450
Have you really thought this through?

885
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,880
If you move to Guangzhou,

886
00:40:44,110 --> 00:40:44,880
we won't be able

887
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,230
to hang out anymore.

888
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:47,960
Besides,

889
00:40:48,510 --> 00:40:49,400
do you think

890
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:53,110
they even have lollipops
like ours over there?

891
00:40:55,030 --> 00:40:56,230
My mom wants me to go.

892
00:40:59,150 --> 00:41:00,800
If you really don't want to,

893
00:41:01,360 --> 00:41:03,490
just make a fuss about it with your mom.

894
00:41:04,190 --> 00:41:05,760
When my parents make me do something

895
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:07,400
I really don't want to do,

896
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:08,590
I throw a fit.

897
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:09,800
Then they

898
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,030
stop pushing me.

899
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:15,110
Mom says my condition

900
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:16,840
might get better if I move there.

901
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:18,040
I want to give it a try.

902
00:41:18,710 --> 00:41:20,110
After all, when winter comes here,

903
00:41:20,110 --> 00:41:21,590
I can't even go outside.

904
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:25,110
All right.

905
00:41:25,590 --> 00:41:27,280
Lollipops are on me today.

906
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:28,030
Okay.

907
00:41:28,710 --> 00:41:29,920
I'll treat you next time.

908
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:30,710
Deal.

909
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:42,800
All right.

910
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:43,800
As long as

911
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:45,730
you've really thought it through.

912
00:41:48,550 --> 00:41:49,550
What are you

913
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:51,010
planning to do in Beijing?

914
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:53,150
I'm thinking

915
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:57,550
of getting involved
in a medical equipment project.

916
00:41:57,550 --> 00:41:59,360
I'll just be lending a hand
behind the scenes.

917
00:41:59,360 --> 00:42:00,440
You could say

918
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:03,490
I'll still be saving lives,
just indirectly.

919
00:42:05,030 --> 00:42:05,840
Sounds good.

920
00:42:06,110 --> 00:42:08,170
Working behind the scenes suits you.

921
00:42:11,510 --> 00:42:12,640
Do you remember how,

922
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:13,550
whenever someone

923
00:42:13,550 --> 00:42:15,000
picked on me as a kid,

924
00:42:15,320 --> 00:42:16,110
you'd come charging out

925
00:42:16,110 --> 00:42:17,400
of some random corner

926
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:18,590
to stand up for me?

927
00:42:18,710 --> 00:42:19,590
Come on, let's not talk about that.

928
00:42:19,590 --> 00:42:21,120
Seriously! It was amazing!

929
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:29,370
Liu Zhengliang,

930
00:42:30,920 --> 00:42:32,720
you don't look down on me, do you?

931
00:42:34,190 --> 00:42:36,120
When have I ever looked down on you?

932
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:39,090
How does that saying go?

933
00:42:40,230 --> 00:42:41,960
No matter where life takes you,

934
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:45,150
we'll always be brothers.

935
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:58,290
When are we coming back here again?

936
00:43:00,880 --> 00:43:01,710
Anytime.
